import json
from pathlib import Path
p=Path('/workspace/sites/arraystep/dist')
rows=[
('Python lists','Foundation','Lists keep values in order. Indices start at zero. Mutating a list changes that object; slicing creates a shallow copy.','a = [4, 7, 2]\na.append(9)\nprint(a[0], a[-1])  # 4 9\nprint(a[1:3])       # [7, 2]','What is [4, 7, 2][-1]?',['4','7','2'],2,'O(1) indexing; O(n) slicing','Running Sum of 1d Array','running-sum-of-1d-array'),
('Traversal & invariants','Foundation','Visit every element once. An invariant describes what your variables mean after each iteration. Here total equals the sum of the values visited so far.','def array_sum(nums):\n    total = 0\n    for x in nums:\n        total += x\n    return total','How many visits for n elements?',['n','n²','log n'],0,'O(n) time, O(1) extra space','Max Consecutive Ones','max-consecutive-ones'),
('Complexity & edge cases','Foundation','Count operations as the input grows. Test empty input, one item, duplicates and negative values. Two nested full traversals usually take quadratic time.','def has_pair(nums, target):\n    for i in range(len(nums)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(nums)):\n            if nums[i] + nums[j] == target:\n                return True\n    return False','Worst-case time of this pair search?',['O(n)','O(n²)','O(1)'],1,'O(n²) time, O(1) space','Contains Duplicate','contains-duplicate'),
('Hash sets & duplicates','Core','A set records values already seen. Check membership before insertion to detect a repeated value. Set operations take average constant time.','def has_duplicate(nums):\n    seen = set()\n    for x in nums:\n        if x in seen:\n            return True\n        seen.add(x)\n    return False','What input contains a duplicate?',['[1, 2, 3]','[1, 2, 1]','[]'],1,'O(n) average time, O(n) space','Contains Duplicate','contains-duplicate'),
('Hash maps & Two Sum','Core','Store each value with its index. Before storing the current value, look for target minus that value. This avoids using the same index twice.','def two_sum(nums, target):\n    seen = {}\n    for i, x in enumerate(nums):\n        if target - x in seen:\n            return [seen[target - x], i]\n        seen[x] = i\n    return []','For x=3 and target=8, look for…',['3','5','8'],1,'O(n) average time, O(n) space','Two Sum','two-sum'),
('Two pointers','Core','For a sorted array, move the left pointer right when the sum is too small. Move the right pointer left when it is too large. Sorting first changes the original indices.','def pair_sorted(a, target):\n    left, right = 0, len(a) - 1\n    while left < right:\n        s = a[left] + a[right]\n        if s == target:\n            return [left, right]\n        if s < target:\n            left += 1\n        else:\n            right -= 1\n    return []','This sum-based pointer rule needs…',['A sorted array','Only positive numbers','Unique elements'],0,'O(n) time, O(1) space','Two Sum II - Input Array Is Sorted','two-sum-ii-input-array-is-sorted'),
('In-place write pointer','Core','Keep a write position for accepted values. Read every input once and compact the values you want to keep. The suffix beyond the returned length is irrelevant.','def remove_value(nums, val):\n    write = 0\n    for x in nums:\n        if x != val:\n            nums[write] = x\n            write += 1\n    return write','What does write count?',['Removed values','Kept values','All comparisons'],1,'O(n) time, O(1) space','Remove Element','remove-element'),
('Fixed sliding window','Patterns','Add the entering element and remove the leaving element. Maintain exactly k elements when evaluating a window. This avoids summing each window again.','def max_window_sum(a, k):\n    if not 1 <= k <= len(a):\n        raise ValueError("invalid k")\n    total = sum(a[:k])\n    best = total\n    for r in range(k, len(a)):\n        total += a[r] - a[r-k]\n        best = max(best, total)\n    return best','After advancing, remove…',['The entering item','The previous leftmost item','The largest item'],1,'O(n) time, O(1) space','Maximum Average Subarray I','maximum-average-subarray-i'),
('Variable sliding window','Patterns','For positive numbers, expand right until the sum reaches the target, then shrink left while valid. Negative values break the monotonic sum rule used here.','def min_length(a, target):\n    left = total = 0\n    best = len(a) + 1\n    for right, x in enumerate(a):\n        total += x\n        while total >= target:\n            best = min(best, right-left+1)\n            total -= a[left]\n            left += 1\n    return 0 if best > len(a) else best','This implementation assumes…',['Positive target and positive elements','Any negative elements','A sorted array'],0,'O(n) time, O(1) space','Minimum Size Subarray Sum','minimum-size-subarray-sum'),
('Prefix sums','Patterns','Let prefix[i] be the sum before index i. The sum of the half-open interval [left, right) is prefix[right] minus prefix[left].','def prefixes(a):\n    p = [0]\n    for x in a:\n        p.append(p[-1] + x)\n    return p\n\np = prefixes([2, 4, 6])\nprint(p[3] - p[1])  # 10','Sum of [left, right) is…',['p[right]-p[left]','p[right]+p[left]','p[left]-p[right]'],0,'O(n) preprocessing, O(1) query','Range Sum Query - Immutable','range-sum-query-immutable'),
('Prefix sum + frequency map','Patterns','A previous prefix equal to current minus k makes a subarray with sum k. Store frequencies because identical prefix sums may appear multiple times. Works with negatives too.','def count_sum(a, k):\n    counts = {0: 1}\n    total = answer = 0\n    for x in a:\n        total += x\n        answer += counts.get(total-k, 0)\n        counts[total] = counts.get(total, 0) + 1\n    return answer','Why start with {0: 1}?',['Count subarrays starting at index 0','Skip zero values','Sort the array'],0,'O(n) average time, O(n) space','Subarray Sum Equals K','subarray-sum-equals-k'),
('Binary search','Patterns','Maintain a sorted half-open search interval [lo, hi). Remove the half that cannot contain the target. Each iteration roughly halves the interval.','def search(a, target):\n    lo, hi = 0, len(a)\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if a[mid] < target:\n            lo = mid + 1\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return lo if lo < len(a) and a[lo] == target else -1','Each step reduces the interval by about…',['One item','Half','Nothing'],1,'O(log n) time, O(1) space','Binary Search','binary-search'),
('Kadane & dynamic programming','Advanced','The best subarray ending here either starts here or extends the previous best ending here. Initialize from the first element so all-negative inputs work.','def max_subarray(a):\n    if not a:\n        raise ValueError("empty array")\n    current = best = a[0]\n    for x in a[1:]:\n        current = max(x, current + x)\n        best = max(best, current)\n    return best','For [-5, -2, -8], the answer is…',['0','-2','-15'],1,'O(n) time, O(n) slicing space in this version','Maximum Subarray','maximum-subarray'),
('Sort & merge intervals','Advanced','Sort intervals by start. Merge an interval with the last result if they overlap; otherwise start a new result. Here touching endpoints count as overlap.','def merge(intervals):\n    out = []\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals):\n        if out and start <= out[-1][1]:\n            out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            out.append([start, end])\n    return out','Merge [1,3] and [2,5] gives…',['[1,5]','[2,3]','Two intervals'],0,'O(n log n) time, O(n) space','Merge Intervals','merge-intervals'),
('Monotonic stack','Advanced','Keep unresolved indices on a stack. When a warmer temperature arrives, resolve smaller temperatures from the top. Each index is pushed and popped at most once.','def warmer(t):\n    out = [0] * len(t)\n    stack = []\n    for i, x in enumerate(t):\n        while stack and t[stack[-1]] < x:\n            j = stack.pop()\n            out[j] = i-j\n        stack.append(i)\n    return out','Why is the nested while still linear?',['Each index pops at most once','It is not linear','The array is sorted'],0,'O(n) time, O(n) space','Daily Temperatures','daily-temperatures'),
('Matrix traversal','Advanced','A matrix is a list of rows. Validate rectangular shape when needed. For a clockwise rotation of an n by n matrix, transpose then reverse each row.','def rotate(square):\n    n = len(square)\n    if any(len(row) != n for row in square):\n        raise ValueError("must be square")\n    for r in range(n):\n        for c in range(r+1, n):\n            square[r][c], square[c][r] = square[c][r], square[r][c]\n    for row in square:\n        row.reverse()','Clockwise rotation uses…',['Transpose then reverse rows','Only transpose','Only reverse rows'],0,'O(n²) time, O(1) extra space','Rotate Image','rotate-image'),
('Greedy reachability','Advanced','Keep the furthest reachable index. If an index lies beyond that frontier, it cannot be reached. Update the frontier using each reachable jump length. Assume nonnegative jumps.','def can_jump(a):\n    reach = 0\n    for i, jump in enumerate(a):\n        if i > reach:\n            return False\n        reach = max(reach, i+jump)\n    return bool(a)','If i exceeds reach, you should…',['Return False','Keep jumping','Sort the input'],0,'O(n) time, O(1) space','Jump Game','jump-game'),
('Binary search on the answer','Advanced','When feasibility is monotonic, search the answer space. For nonnegative workloads, ask if a capacity can split the array into at most k contiguous groups.','def split_limit(a, k):\n    if not a or not 1 <= k <= len(a) or min(a) < 0:\n        raise ValueError("invalid input")\n    lo, hi = max(a), sum(a)\n    while lo < hi:\n        mid = (lo+hi)//2\n        groups, total = 1, 0\n        for x in a:\n            if total+x > mid:\n                groups += 1\n                total = 0\n            total += x\n        if groups <= k:\n            hi = mid\n        else:\n            lo = mid+1\n    return lo','If capacity increases, required groups…',['Cannot increase','Must increase','Always become one'],0,'O(n log(sum(a)-max(a)+1)) time, O(1) space','Split Array Largest Sum','split-array-largest-sum')]
data=[dict(zip(['title','level','lesson','code','question','options','answer','complexity','problem','slug'],r)) for r in rows]
(p/'lessons.json').write_text(json.dumps(data))
